# Line endings
#
# This repo is CRLF nearly throughout (~180 of 210 text files). Nothing declared
# that, so line endings depended on whatever tool last wrote a file — which is
# how commit 3cacd11 ended up rewriting six files end to end when only a few
# hundred lines actually changed.
#
# Pinning eol=crlf keeps checkouts and fresh clones consistent with what is
# already on disk, and makes git warn ("LF will be replaced by CRLF") as soon as
# a file drifts from the convention.
#
# Note what this does NOT do: because the committed blobs still hold CRLF, a
# tool that rewrites a file as LF will still produce a whole-file diff. Closing
# that hole means normalising the stored blobs to LF:
#
#     git add --renormalize . && git commit -m "normalize line endings"
#
# after which both LF and CRLF working copies diff clean. That is a one-time
# ~180-file commit, which is why it has not been done here.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Binaries must never be line-ending converted.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.wav   binary
*.jar   binary
*.keystore binary
*.p8    binary
*.p12   binary
